it's been one week since i dove deep  into the brand new galaxy fold 4 and its  accessories testing out samsung's  ecosystem after being stuck in apples  for many years so here are my honest  thoughts and opinions now last year with  a full three i was really disappointed  and fairly harsh in my review so do i  still hate samsung's foldables or have  things changed well honestly i really  only have a few complaints so let's dive  in the design of the fold is fantastic  the quality is top notch the hinge is  much improved and the seam that is still  here isn't noticeable day to day it's  weird saying that something actually  feels higher quality than my 13 pro but  it does it is very solid now on this  side right here with this front screen  this is one area that i complained about  last year this has been much improved we  have a full size screen here it is  really bright and it could go all the  way down to one hertz which saves a lot  of battery that's gonna be important in  a second as far as usability i really  like how narrow the phone is and it's  very comfortable to hold in the hand  even though it is thick and then when  you open it up compared to last year way  more apps are optimized and work  properly whereas before someone even go  full screen i absolutely love the bar  here at the bottom so you can quickly  switch to a different application the  first time i used it was actually  completely by accident and then it hit  me wow i literally just did that  naturally and it's so quick for the apps  that you use often overall the whole  phone is extremely fast with that  updated snapdragon processor now of  course on the cpu not much has changed  but as far as graphics it has gotten  much better and playing games on the  fold 4 is amazing with this large screen  there's no slowdowns heat is not an  issue it's a great experience but for my  favorite game which is call of duty and  probably others like it it actually  isn't great  not because the visuals aren't good it's  because of the aspect ratio certain  things on the sides get cut out and  there'd be people opponents that i  straight up would not see compared to a  regular wide phone now as for regular  use i want to talk briefly about the new  watch i think this is the first android  watch in a long time that is actually  good performance is great i like the  look of it the only issue is that it's  kind of thick and i don't love the  controls that it's all touch screen and  then that we have these buttons we don't  have that dial anymore but the battery  life is ridiculous you can go two full  days and you still have some extra power  compared to my apple watch which only  does about one day and then if you're  using things like maps uh or you're  doing a lot of active tracking for  workouts it could be half a day and it's  gone so i think android other than the  design the watches are finally at a  point where they do work well and if  you're using a samsung phone and you  want a smart watch don't hesitate i  think you'll enjoy it now there's a  couple more things that really surprised  me about the fold the first are the  speakers they were pretty good last year  but this year they are amazing beats my  iphone and the pro max version in every  single way loudness bass samsung has  done a really good job so if you're  watching videos if you're listening to  music  the experience is wonderful and of  course you can cup them that way the  sound actually bounces off your hands  right into your ears instead of being  front facing and both speakers are the  same and with that the video quality as  well now this is a large screen and  square so yes if you zoom in some stuff  gets cut out but even without zooming in  the the size of the video is still  bigger than the 13 pro max the hdr also  looks better it is brighter more  contrast the visual experience is  fantastic  now with that i want to bring in these  headphones as well  these buds 2 pro are amazing i've been  using airpods pro ever since they came  out and each time samsung releases new  earbuds they keep getting better and  these now are better than the airpods  pro in almost every single way the sound  quality amazing microphones have been  much improved noise cancellation is  better i was flying uh with them and i  actually didn't use my airpods max i was  just using these um comfort is really  good i think up to three hours that's  really the only downside where after  about three hours i start getting some  pain around where they touch my ear  but other than that i mean samsung is  really killing it and no samsung did not  provide any of these products for us to  review we bought all of them so earbuds  fantastic now of course if you're using  with your iphone you don't have all the  extra features that i love so that is a  downside there but getting back to the  fold i want to talk about the cameras  because last year they were not good  this year though we have had a huge  upgrade and in our blind camera  comparison  the fold 4 actually beat out the s22  ultra updated and the iphone as well  uh it doesn't have that telephoto shot  so sometimes it did worse but overall  the images look great the portrait shots  are amazing  even the inside camera even though i  typically wouldn't use it it's gotten a  lot better and i've been using it to  have to use face unlock it works fast  every time very consistent so there's no  longer a compromise spending way more  money but getting worse cameras because  they were great and i think the 50  megapixel camera it actually does better  for processing because it's a lot less  pixels and then with it for video the  video actually looks pretty good as well  because with the s22 ultra i mean you're  just throwing away so much data where  this one it looks good now the only  thing i would say is that sometimes it's  a little too over saturated a little bit  over sharpened as far as the video but  samsung's definitely come a long way  still not the level of the video on the  iphone that's definitely a head  but they are heading in the right  direction and the last thing that  surprised me was the battery life the  battery is larger in here there's a lot  more optimizations better processor the  screens go lower as far as the frequency  and you get eight to nine hours of mid  to heavy use and that's very surprising  so it's no longer a downgrade and then  with that  the one thing that i kind of found is  that after about three days or so i  ended up using the front screen way more  often because it's way more usable now  so i would say towards the end of that  week i was using probably 80 the front  screen and then really opening it up  when i needed that larger display and at  that point the battery life got even  better and that's when i started kind of  questioning do i really need a foldable  phone if only twenty percent of time i'm  using this screen here and i'm  preferring the normal phone like i have  in years past kind of the novelty  started to wear off  and with that the s pen didn't get that  much use now one reason is just because  it there's no spot for it you know you  have that extra case that samsung has  that makes it a lot more bulky it  doesn't feel great in your pocket and a  few times i just left it here and then i  went on a trip and i also left it as  well i think if there's one thing that  could make this better it would just be  to have the s pen built in even if that  means a little bit worse battery life uh  if they have to you know make some space  for that pen it would just take it up  just another level to have it with you  at all times and with that we have of  course the price people expected  foldable phones to come down in price  after they've been out a couple years  but they haven't this thing's still very  expensive now samsung does give you  sales they'll give you some accessories  uh they'll give you a larger storage  capacity if you pre-ordered but that's  